<title>ISRAEL: Africa Israel Q2 EPS plunges.</title>
<headline>Africa Israel Q2 EPS plunges.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Africa Israel Investments, a subsidiary of Bank Leumi.</p>
<p>			 (In thousands of shekels except EPS)</p>
<p>			 Q2 96	 Q2 95	6-MTH 96    6-MTH 95</p>
<p>Revenue		333,494     209,136    581,137     338,885</p>
<p>Net profit	    33,140	34,052     72,543	59,728</p>
<p>from regular</p>
<p>operations</p>
<p>(including insurance)</p>
<p>Net profit	     3,594	26,549     38,584	 56,978</p>
<p>EPS			7.88	 57.37	83.60	 123.37</p>
<p>The results were negatively affected by a provision of 9.0 million shekels for fines that may be imposed on the company's insurance subsidiaries for alleged cartel activities.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
